    "title": "Chatty gibbon has fun with caretaker in Yunnan - Chinadaily.com.cn",
    "text": "A white-browed gibbon at Taiyanghe National Forest Park in Pu'er, Yunnan province, recently had a warm interaction with his caretaker, capturing the attention of netizens.\nOn the way to the next destination, Dingding clung to the wrist of staff member Xu Yanfang and called out in response to her, creating a heartwarming scene.\nDingding is a national first-class protected wild animal who enjoys the company of red pandas, rhinoceroses, and Asian bearcats, spending his days playing with them throughout the park.",
